# R session / working-state artifacts - never intentional output
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj
*.Rout
Rplots.pdf

# Large, fully re-fetchable raw source data - regenerate with the
# scripts in Fetch/ instead of committing. NOT needed at all if you
# never delete the committed derived caches below (see README).
Data/infra_index_source/
Data/wetland_map_source/
Data/nin_data/

# Quick-test artifacts - not real results.
Results_TEST_AOI/
*.real_backup

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# LICENCE EXCLUSION - read before adding anything under these paths.
#
# The AR5 variant is computed from FKB-AR5, whose Geonorge metadata states
# "Nedlasting av data begrenset til Norge Digitalt avtaleparter" (download
# restricted to Norge digitalt parties, Norge digitalt-lisens, Geovekst).
# Its derived wetland OUTLINES are therefore not ours to redistribute:
# they are area-preserving, only lightly generalised (2 m), and national,
# so publishing them would effectively republish FKB-AR5 geometry.
#
# What IS published from the AR5 variant: the aggregated results - region
# and national indicator values, the region-level map, the values tables
# and the metadata. Those are statistics, not geometry.
#
# Anyone with AR5 access regenerates the geometry locally with
# run_connectivity_ar5.ps1. Anyone without it gets the same pipeline on
# AR50 (NIBIO, open data, NLOD), which Fetch/prepare_ar5_mire_regions.R
# falls back to automatically - AR50-derived outputs carry no such
# restriction and may be published.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Data/wetland_map_ar5/
Data/connectivity_output_ar5/
Deliverables/NO_CONN_001_indicatorMap_polygon.rds

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Size exclusions (not licence): the ~2GB of derived caches for the
# mire-model variant. Several exceed GitHub's 100MB per-file hard limit,
# and keeping 2GB out of git history keeps the repo quick to clone. They
# are published as GitHub Release assets instead and retrieved by
# Fetch/download_caches.R - see README's "Cache vs. real compute"
# section. Regenerating them from scratch is 20+ hours of compute, so do
# not delete them casually.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Data/LUI_output/
Data/wetland_map_simplified/
Data/connectivity_output_simplified/

# The mire-model variant's polygon-level map (1.15 M rows, 51 MB). Excluded
# for SIZE only - it derives from open sources (mire probability model +
# NiN) and may be redistributed; Main/export_deliverables.R regenerates it.
Deliverables_MireModel/NO_CONN_001_indicatorMap_polygon.rds

# Scored polygons written by Fetch/scale_and_map_connectivity_indicator.R
# (450 MB mire-model / 712 MB AR5; minutes to regenerate). The variant
# documentation in that folder IS committed.
Data/connectivity_scored/*
!Data/connectivity_scored/README_variants.md
!Data/connectivity_scored/run_logs_AR5/
